{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/103519-abyssals-are-not-doomed-enough","id":103519,"title":"Abyssals are not doomed enough.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-01T11:34:06-07:00","id":103519,"title":"Abyssals are not doomed enough.","content":"I know that Abyssals have sometimes felt like the black sheep of 2e, and I think we all know the reason: They are not doomed enough. It was too easy to play a 2e Abyssal and, by simply never creating life or disobeying your Deathlord or falling in love or answering to your name or using your Unexpected-remover or resisting UMI, live a mostly-normal life as long as you don't mind never regenerating Essence in Creation and paying WP for several of your most important charms. You could fall in love and the person you loved might never get murdered by the Neverborn using a fiat-level power against which there is no defense!<br /> <br /> Obviously this drove people away from Abyssals, so I think we need to brainstorm some fixes. For example: Every time an Abyssal uses anyone's name, something they have an intimacy to dissolves into bitter dust and ashes. STs are advised to adjudicate this rule carefully to prevent abuse -- some players may choose their intimacies to target opponents, or to avoid having an intimacy to the things that actually make the game fun for them! Do not let them get away with this. Determine what they enjoy and have it turn to dust and ashes immediately. If the player persists in having fun, you may declare that their character dissolves into dust and ashes. But this is not an escape! They must continue to play a pile of dust and ashes for the remainder of the game; they may not create a new character.<br /> <br /> In 2e it was too easy to vent resonance. Therefore, 3e should fix this: In 3e your resonance can never go down ever. An Abyssal who reaches 10 resonance simply continues to experience a full-scale resonance eruption every tick forever.<br /> <br /> Other characters should intuitively understand that the Abyssal is evil; when they meet them, they should declare their hatred and disgust with the Abyssal in a loud tone of voice. This is unnatural mental influence costing 1 WP a scene to resist.<br /> <br /> Every action an Abyssal takes, without exception, brings the world closer to its doom. The ST should constantly keep private notes of every single thing Abyssal characters do in a session; then, at the end of the session, pull them aside and go over every single action, explaining how each one helped doom the world a little bit more. (&quot;Twelve seconds into the session, you said 'hi'. These words were overheard by an invisible spirit in the corner of the room, reminding him of his dead love and driving him over the edge. He immediately rampaged out and killed...&quot;)<br /> <br /> Whispers also work differently now. They represent the irrevocable and irresistible taint of the Neverborn on your soul. All Abyssals must have at least Whispers 1, and it increases by 1 every scene, as well as every time they botch a roll or succeed a roll or fail a roll. It is not limited by the usual limit of 5 for backgrounds. Your whispers rating connects your mind to the Neverborn, constantly filling it with their gibbering madness and allowing them to take total control over you a number of times per scene equal to your Whispers rating, for as long as they want. Since the Deathlords have your monstrance, they may do so as well (their limit for controlling you is counted separately from the Neverborn.)<br /> <br /> I know this probably isn't enough to make Abyssals really, truly doomed, so let's hear if anyone else has any suggestions to enhance the Abyssal &quot;doomed&quot; experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 04-01-2014, 03:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":18}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T11:46:24-07:00","id":103529,"title":"","content":"Abyssals should gain Resonance whenever they apply any if their DVs against anything. This is to highlight how living as an Abyssal is the most selfish choice of all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T11:46:58-07:00","id":103531,"title":"","content":"Well, in my games, you had to purchase all Charms as Taints. If a Charm didn't have a Taint, it now does for double the EXP of the Charm and providing a random mutation. Also, Taints should be only aesthetic, providing no bonuses, and you still need to activate the Charm as normal. And, of course, activating a Charm counts as a sin against the Neverborn, and increases your Resonance.<br /> <br /> Anima powers, we felt, were also not doomy enough, for the players or the characters, so we merged them into a single power that strangled the Abyssal the more motes they spent. At the 11+ mote level, you passed out, and any action you were about to perform is terminated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T11:58:17-07:00","id":103536,"title":"","content":"Every time an abyssal kills someone by any method (including their resonance vent), that person's ghost is permanently bound to the Abyssal's mind and flesh. These ghosts death screams resound eternally in their mind, giving a penalty on any mental action not related to killing something equal to the total number of bound ghosts. Killing a sentient being removes this penalty for a scene, as the old ghosts pester the new one for a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T12:01:03-07:00","id":103538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/103519-abyssals-are-not-doomed-enough#post103519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that Abyssals have sometimes felt like the black sheep of 2e, and I think we all know the reason: They are not doomed enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are sufficiently doomed that I have no intention of ever playing one. Too much Gothic melodrama and Hot Topic merchandise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T12:08:04-07:00","id":103541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/103519-abyssals-are-not-doomed-enough#post103519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example: Every time an Abyssal uses anyone's name, something they have an intimacy to dissolves into bitter dust and ashes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe that's why their own names tend to sound like elaborate misdirections? Very interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T12:11:32-07:00","id":103548,"title":"","content":"Your irony is so deliciously poisonous it's befitting an Abyssal charm of it's own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2052,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","user":"FromBeyond","date":". 04-01-2014, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T12:11:52-07:00","id":103549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/103519-abyssals-are-not-doomed-enough?p=103538#post103538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are sufficiently doomed that I have no intention of ever playing one. Too much Gothic melodrama and Hot Topic merchandise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone here didn't understand the topic and the date of which <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/239565-wizard-s-panoply-how-to-play-a-mage-in-exalted-collection-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Complete the Wizard's Panoply</a></b> [How to be a mage in Creation]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/442-nephtys","name":"Nephtys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar442_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T12:16:39-07:00","id":103554,"title":"","content":"Every morning, after the Abyssal wakes up, a hungry ghost pops out of the Underworld, kills the nearest mortal and uses their blood to write detailed instructions for the Abyssal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T12:19:14-07:00","id":103559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephtys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/103519-abyssals-are-not-doomed-enough?p=103549#post103549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone here didn't understand the topic and the date of which <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't blame him, I almost missed that myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T12:20:38-07:00","id":103563,"title":"","content":"I've got some ideas!<br /> <br /> First off, Soulsteel's got to go. It's not really <i>gruesome</i> enough, y'know? It's practically just Starmetal, only made out of mortals rather than gods. Lame. Instead, I propose that we give them a new focus on the sadly-ignored necrotech. In fact, let's require all Abyssals to exclusively use necrotech artifacts!<br /> <br /> But necrotech's only an aesthetic. If we want that feeling of bleak despair to <b>really</b> hit home, we should require that necrotech artifacts be made of the Abyssal's family. Only blood relatives (maybe wives, but that's sort of stepping on the Ebon Dragon's stuff) can be forged into necrotech weapons and armor! This will highlight the dark, mature themes of the Abyssal Exalted and really connect players to the narrative significance of their attire.<br /> <br /> Next up, Blasphemy. This keyword was mostly introduced for the Infernal Exalted, but I'm seeing a real opportunity to step it up a notch with <b>Super Blasphemy.</b> This keyword not only alerts the Sidereals and all beings in the area that you've used a charm, it also marks your current location for the next week and sextuples the speed of all pursuers. This will create a palpable feeling of opposition, allowing Abyssals the chance to fight literally everything in Creation. To expedite this, I propose this keyword be attached to all Abyssal charms.<br /> <br /> Finally, let's spice things up a bit. Abyssals are meant to draw from vampiric themes, but they're lacking so many narratively interesting traits! I propose traditional weaknesses, such as an inability to cross running water, deathly fear of the sun and unhideable Transylvanian accent be grafted on to the splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/789-mercury","name":"Mercury","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T12:27:20-07:00","id":103567,"title":"","content":"I think part of the problem is that Abyssals don't regenerate Essence in Creation and they can only regenerate it in the Underworld.<br /> <br /> To fix this, I suggest that while in Creation Abyssals have 0 motes and instead pay mote costs in aggravated health levels. While in the Underworld Abyssals have their motes but can never regain them, because creating motes is creation and that would be against the way of death. An Abyssal only has the number of motes they start with at character generation for the entire duration of the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T12:44:05-07:00","id":103577,"title":"","content":"The player can only gain stunt bonuses if they cut themselves and bleed on their character sheet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T12:52:27-07:00","id":103587,"title":"","content":"Obvious, the Spectral keyword isn't limiting enough; just 1 WP to use those charms outside of the Underworld? <i>Puh</i>-lease.<br /> <br /> I suggest that every time they use a Spectral charm, they gain 1 Resonance, and the player is required to turn to the ST and say &quot;Thank you sir, may I please have another?&quot;<br /> <br /> EDIT: This is, of course, assuming the ST is playing with the utterly balanced and enjoyable rules posited earlier in this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":"would make a hilarious charm? 04-01-2014, 03:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T13:15:23-07:00","id":103613,"title":"","content":"In addition the resonance track, every Abyssal should have an Overwatch score. For every charm they activate and for each hour they spend outside of a shadowland or the Underworld, their Overwatch score increases by 1. Players can decrease their Overwatch scores by means of self-mutilation if they are not in Creation. Each point of lethal damage done by self-harm lowers the Overwatch score by 1.<br /> <br /> If the Overwatch score reaches 100, the Unconquered Sun will annihilate the character with orbital bombardment from the Daystar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T14:25:14-07:00","id":103637,"title":"","content":"100's an awful lot. This isn't Yugioh.<br /> <br /> 10 points Overwatch max.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T14:37:24-07:00","id":103642,"title":"","content":"I'd really prefer it if Abyssals were not hopelessly crippling and depressing to play.<br /> <br /> Abyssals should have an element of tragedy and darkness within them, but that should be as much something you can struggle with as something you can accept. The problem with Abyssals used to be that either you were a nihilistic shithead who wanted to wipe out reality, or you redeemed yourself. Those things should be possible for Abyssal, but granularity is important. You should be able to play a whole gamut of Abyssal characters between those very far extremes, including characters with much the same motivations as Solars and Lunars and DBs and everyone else, who happened to Exalt as an Abyssal because you don't get to pick what colour the sun on your forehead shines.<br /> <br /> Death Knight in aesthetic, champion of virtue in reality is a character I always wanted to play, without having to sacrifice the Death Knight aesthetic to do it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T14:41:22-07:00","id":103646,"title":"","content":"Do remember what day it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T14:42:05-07:00","id":103648,"title":"","content":"This is a thread of unbound spite and disdain for the old Abyssal paradigm. Do not bring serious considerations of Abyssal development into it.<br /> <br /> (I'm all for a proper Abyssal discussion thread, though.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T14:44:22-07:00","id":103650,"title":"","content":"Playing an Abyssal gives your ST permission to literally punch you in the face if they think you are having fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T14:50:22-07:00","id":103653,"title":"","content":"Nah, you're all thinking way too small about this. Abyssals are the bringers of inevitable doom afterall. To this end, their Resonance should be altered in such a way that any action that would generate resonance, instead generates 10. And once at 10 resonance, no wimpy &quot;boo hoo I create a shadowland&quot; bs. Screw it, everything - <i>everything</i> - within 100 miles x Essence instantly dies, including ghosts, zombies (they DOUBLE die) and the ground, as a tremendous surge of Void bursts through their exaltation.<br /> <br /> Of course, the only things spared by this effect would be necrotech artifacts and blood relatives (as you'll need those for your next necrotech artifacts).<br /> <br /> To high-light their victorian/gothic themes, as they are the princes/princesses of the underworld, the only way they can regain HP is by leeches. They'll regain one bashing point per hour for every 3 leeches they currently have attached to them, a lethal every 7 and an aggravated every 20. These are no ordinary leeches however, they are zombie leeches created through necrosurgery, as normal leeches would just cause some bleeding damage - nobody wants that.<br /> <br /> Lastly, they can't stand ANY light, as it damages their fragile complection. All abyssals are now required to walk with a necrotech lolita-goth parasol (usually made from the skins of their children), lest they take 1 aggravated damage per tick from any light source.<br /> <br /> ((edit: crap, I actually like that leeches idea ))<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 04-01-2014, 06:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T15:01:46-07:00","id":103657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/103519-abyssals-are-not-doomed-enough?p=103653#post103653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, you're all thinking way too small about this. Abyssals are the bringers of inevitable doom afterall. To this end, their Resonance should be altered in such a way that any action that would generate resonance, instead generates 10. And once at 10 resonance, no wimpy &quot;boo hoo I create a shadowland&quot; bs. Screw it, everything - <i>everything</i> - within 100 miles x Essence instantly dies, including ghosts, zombies (they DOUBLE die) and the ground, as a tremendous surge of Void bursts through their exaltation.<br /> <br /> Of course, the only things spared by this effect would be necrotech artifacts and blood relatives (as you'll need those for your next necrotech artifacts).</div> </div> </div> </div>I say why bother? Let's just say that the Void surge automatically converts all of your blood relatives in the radius into necrotech artifacts instantly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T15:11:44-07:00","id":103661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/103519-abyssals-are-not-doomed-enough?p=103657#post103657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I say why bother? Let's just say that the Void surge automatically converts all of your blood relatives in the radius into necrotech artifacts instantly.</div> </div> </div> </div>That being said, it's important not to gimp characters that are running out of blood relatives (or had very few to begin with). To this end, they should be able to &quot;Sire&quot; half-castes by draining any human (DBs included, because sereously, who cares about those guys?) of blood, and replacing it with the abyssal's, effectively extending their Blood Relatives pool to include all the blood relatives of the sired &quot;childe&quot;.<br /> <br /> Whew, Nipped <i>that</i> problem in the bud.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T15:23:58-07:00","id":103670,"title":"","content":"And I just finished rereading that thread where I cross posted some stuff from TVTropes. It was a while ago that happened, but my first thought was that this was a sarcastic reaction to that. It probably isn't, but I'm still tempted to link this to TVTropes' Exalted thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T15:28:19-07:00","id":103672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/103519-abyssals-are-not-doomed-enough?p=103661#post103661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That being said, it's important not to gimp characters that are running out of blood relatives (or had very few to begin with). To this end, they should be able to &quot;Sire&quot; half-castes by draining any human (DBs included, because sereously, who cares about those guys?) of blood, and replacing it with the abyssal's, effectively extending their Blood Relatives pool to include all the blood relatives of the sired &quot;childe&quot;.<br /> <br /> Whew, Nipped <i>that</i> problem in the bud.</div> </div> </div> </div>Branching off of that, I posit we should make a background &quot;Blood Relatives&quot; that works like followers, except all the people purchased with it are your actual relatives, thus a perfect fodder for necrotech!<br /> <br /> That will surely convey the message of tragedy, gloom and mature theme of gothic horror perfectly!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T15:36:42-07:00","id":103675,"title":"","content":"But how far does blood relatives go?<br /> <br /> Any of your direct ancestors or descendants would count, easy. Siblings fit into there pretty well, too. But what about Nephews and Nieces? Aunts and Uncles? How about cousins? How many steps removed can you go before they don't count?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T18:03:52-07:00","id":103740,"title":"","content":"My take on the &quot;Doomed&quot; theme and mechanics of Abyssals in 2e is that these themes were applied so heavily to the splat that they kind of backfire on themselves and become irrelevant. What is the point of being a bane against those you would love and protect if the application of resonance and its effects come up on you so fast that you cant really enter into these relationships in the first place. There are so many ways to gain resonance, that if a Abyssal tried to make any meaningful connections for their own purposes they would just be in a constant state of resonance break. If your storyteller doesn't rein themselves in on the application of these effects there really isn't any way of playing a Abyssal seeking redemption or even just a relatively normal life, the would kill all the crops, livestock, and unborn babies in the area in a couple of days, which i imagine would make it hard to form relationships. I would look to Michael Moorcock's Elric as a good example of how this could work better, every time he comes to care about someone they die because of the dark pacts and influences he relies on, but the key here is that he is allowed to make these relationships in the first place. Elric often spent month and even years with companions, allies, and lovers, before he caused their deaths. Being able to have periods of relative normalcy makes it so much more poignant when your true nature does surface to screw you over.<br /> <br /> The more story driven resonance effects and resonance breaks from &quot;Shards&quot; go a long way towards fixing this problem, and I hope some version of them will be used when the Abyssals get their EX3 splat book! The triggers that cause you to gain resonance are easier to work around, and the impact of your growing resonance though extremely ominous, is not necessarily physically threatening When your resonance finally breaks, the virtue based mind states are impactful and generally a major hindrance to your character, but still open enough for your character to retain some element of themselves throughout.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T18:15:06-07:00","id":103745,"title":"","content":"I like a lot of what I'm seeing here, but my concern is that choosing to play an Abyssal in a mixed circle may not be punitive enough. Everyone should feel like an enemy of Creation is in their midst. Maybe something like a point of Limit for every tick spent not attacking the Abyssal?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T18:15:15-07:00","id":103746,"title":"","content":"Keywords: Ravish, ravage<br /> <br /> Before activating any charm with these keywords, you must justify your trivialization of sexual assault to a group of angry forum posters as part of an extended social challenge. Failure on this challenge means the charm does not activate and you must write a sincere apology for your attempted use of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T18:41:36-07:00","id":103762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Root</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/103519-abyssals-are-not-doomed-enough?p=103745#post103745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like a lot of what I'm seeing here, but my concern is that choosing to play an Abyssal in a mixed circle may not be punitive enough. Everyone should feel like an enemy of Creation is in their midst. Maybe something like a point of Limit for every tick spent not attacking the Abyssal?</div> </div> </div> </div>Any Solar who kills an Abyssal experiences a euphoric rush of knowing that they have eliminated something that should not have existed, causing them to learn 10 new charms immediately for free. Beating an Abyssal into incapacitated without killing them earns you one charm for free, so Solars in mixed circles have an incentive to keep Abyssals alive in order to farm them in the long run. However, killing Abyssals is addictive, imposing a cumulative 1 WP cost to resist the opportunity for each Abyssal you've killed previously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T18:50:29-07:00","id":103765,"title":"","content":"I feel that the Neverborn themselves don't have sufficient influence over the Abyssals. The Deathlords are just Oblivion's middle management, but the Neverborn are the Executives. All Abyssals should share in the unliving nightmare of the slain Titans when they slumber, to better appreciate the urgency of their world-murdering mission. This adds their Whispers rating as an External Penalty to their morning Conviction roll to regain Willpower.<br /> <br /> In Creation, the nightmares of the Neverborn grow distant, but this should be no boon. In Creation, Abyssals derive no rest from sleep, accumulating fatigue penalties as though time in repose were replaced by hard labor, and receiving no daily roll for Willpower recovery.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/103519-abyssals-are-not-doomed-enough?p=103554#post103554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every morning, after the Abyssal wakes up, a hungry ghost pops out of the Underworld, kills the nearest mortal and uses their blood to write detailed instructions for the Abyssal.</div> </div> </div> </div>(The intent of the thread aside, I'd happily buy that as a charm.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please add signature.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/615-the-hanged-man","name":"The Hanged Man","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T21:51:32-07:00","id":103832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/103519-abyssals-are-not-doomed-enough?p=103762#post103762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any Solar who kills an Abyssal experiences a euphoric rush of knowing that they have eliminated something that should not have existed, causing them to learn 10 new charms immediately for free. Beating an Abyssal into incapacitated without killing them earns you one charm for free, so Solars in mixed circles have an incentive to keep Abyssals alive in order to farm them in the long run. However, killing Abyssals is addictive, imposing a cumulative 1 WP cost to resist the opportunity for each Abyssal you've killed previously.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't feel like that's really punitive enough; under that system, one might almost get the impression that having an Abyssal in a mixed circle is a net benefit to the group.<br /> <br /> Instead, I think that the other members of the group, if sleeping at the same time, should get Nightmares as well, and random hungry ghosts coming to menace their loved ones and steal their unattended belongings. (NPCs come and go, but stuff is forever.)<br /> <br /> And if a hungry ghost steals the belongings of a Creation-sider, it should immediately fade away to oblivion with the object in question in tow. If the group lets the Abyssal hang around long enough in Creation, this should also happen to artifacts, manses and nearby geographical features just to drive home the point that the Abyssal is a thing that does not belong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T22:47:56-07:00","id":103854,"title":"","content":"I don't know, not Doom - y enough.<br /> <br /> I think every time they spend a mote, they have to eat a piece of rock salt. Not the character, the player; let them feel the salt of Creation's fields under their tongues!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T22:57:00-07:00","id":103860,"title":"","content":"I know that this is a joke thread, but does Abyssal really that doom-y, in most Abyssal's themes thread I always see two sides, one claim that Resonance is character-wrecking and make you into the DL's bitch while the other side is on the opinion that Second Edition Resonance has no teeth and they can go on a whole story and never build-up Resonance to 10 points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T23:46:29-07:00","id":103873,"title":"","content":"When you play an Abyssal, you're forced to use special d10's where every face is a 1. This is a statement on how everything is awful and will die eventually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/46-oramus","name":"Oramus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar46_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T01:45:26-07:00","id":103913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/103519-abyssals-are-not-doomed-enough?p=103860#post103860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that this is a joke thread, but does Abyssal really that doom-y, in most Abyssal's themes thread I always see two sides, one claim that Resonance is character-wrecking and make you into the DL's bitch while the other side is on the opinion that Second Edition Resonance has no teeth and they can go on a whole story and never build-up Resonance to 10 points.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends so much on the ST. In a mixed circle, you could accumulate Resonance every scene if the ST interprets your actions as building or maintaining positive Intimacies with the living. Cooperation in combat could be interpreted as promoting or defending life - even if you are murdering people, you may offend the Neverborn my murdering people who are trying to kill your living allies. Not April Fools =(","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T04:00:13-07:00","id":103948,"title":"","content":"I think Abyssals should have the 1 again rule to maximize the disaster they bring upon all things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/481-rahsith","name":"rahsith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T06:40:08-07:00","id":104002,"title":"","content":"In a not so far future someone will ressurect this thread and will not understand its sarcasm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/239565-wizard-s-panoply-how-to-play-a-mage-in-exalted-collection-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Complete the Wizard's Panoply</a></b> [How to be a mage in Creation]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/442-nephtys","name":"Nephtys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar442_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T06:53:44-07:00","id":104007,"title":"","content":"I'm contemplating locking it for that very reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T06:55:11-07:00","id":104008,"title":"","content":"I think the 3rd edition Abyssals book needs to have razorblades tapped to the corners of the pages. The pdfs should come with a virus that makes your hard drive overheat and explode. <br /> <br /> It's the only way to adequately represent the agony of being an Abyssal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T11:30:47-07:00","id":104195,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rahsith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/103519-abyssals-are-not-doomed-enough?p=103948#post103948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Abyssals should have the 1 again rule to maximize the disaster they bring upon all things.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Actually, joking aside, this reminds me of the oWoD &quot;each 1 removes one success from your total&quot; rule, which would make for a great Resonance effect (or curse from some spell or Charm).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;We do not quit playing because we grow old, we grow old because we quit playing.&quot; - Oliver Wendell Holmes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","name":"MrInsecure","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T11:37:34-07:00","id":104201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/103519-abyssals-are-not-doomed-enough?p=104008#post104008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the 3rd edition Abyssals book needs to have razorblades tapped to the corners of the pages. The pdfs should come with a virus that makes your hard drive overheat and explode.<br /> <br /> It's the only way to adequately represent the agony of being an Abyssal.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you must learn to <i>endure</i> the pain. The razorblades will be coated in the juices of a <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carolina_Reaper\" target=\"_blank\">Carolina Reaper</a>, and the virus on the PDF will cause your web browser to only open Rick Astley videos and Goatse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;We do not quit playing because we grow old, we grow old because we quit playing.&quot; - Oliver Wendell Holmes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","name":"MrInsecure","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T11:41:43-07:00","id":104210,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I think all of these are wonderful ideas, especially since it also makes the difference between the Infernals and the Abyssals clearer. Now the Infernals take up the spot of the 'corrupted' Solars and the Abyssals are the Broken, The Doomed.<br /> Also, to give them a good connection to their doomed status, every time your essence increases, you have to hold your character sheet in an open flame for a single second, and any parts of it that are burned away aren't things you can use anymore. This symbolized their identity slowly being dragged into Oblivion and them growing closer to their inevitable, permanent demise, in addition, the character throwing away their name and the player burning away the character sheet are a nice symmetry, as both are giving up their role/identity, or who they are in Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T16:27:40-07:00","id":104424,"title":"","content":"Whoooosh...I only skimmed the thread before posting a response, I am ashamed to say I had no idea it was a joke thread, I just really thought people liked their grim abyssal doom LOL.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","user":"turkeygiant","date":". 04-02-2014, 07:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T21:09:26-07:00","id":104574,"title":"","content":"And don't forget, whatever your moniker or title might be, the Neverborn automatically changes every Abyssal's True Name to Luigi. Which is actually why using it gets them Resonance, and is in general responsible for all the doom.<br /> <br /> Edit* As an aside, it should also be noted that all 2nd edition Lunars are also forced to change their original names to Luigi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":697,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","user":"Arteliex","date":". 04-03-2014, 01:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T22:06:35-07:00","id":104602,"title":"","content":"So the Year of Luigi was a Deathlord scheme?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T13:45:50-07:00","id":105063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/103519-abyssals-are-not-doomed-enough?p=103854#post103854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think every time they spend a mote, they have to eat a piece of rock salt. Not the character, the player; let them feel the salt of Creation's fields under their tongues!</div> </div> </div> </div>If they balk at it, feel free to toss in a tablespoon of cinnamon as well to improve the flavor. We're not <i>monsters</i> here.<br /> <br /> (But no water, obviously. That'd defeat the whole point.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1369-mewtarthio","name":"Mewtarthio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}